[14282]="70037A8F\n1\tCapture Dour Hal for questioning\tDour Hal can be found in Fushum Raus. You should do your best to capture Dour Hal and haul him in for questioning.\n2\tSpeak with Húnbrit\tHúnbrit has appeared nearby in Fushum Raus. You should speak with Húnbrit now that Dour Hal has been subdued.\n",
[14283]="70054CA0\n1\tCollect crafter's steel (total: 6)\030Collect worn trinkets (total: 6)\tThese items may be found by defeating foes in Imlad Morgul instances. Different instances will yield different types of items.\n2\tReturn to Tordoron\tYou should deliver the items you collected to Tordoron in Echad Uial.\n",
[14284]="70054CA5\n1\tCollect deep-lichen (total: 6)\030Collect smoothed stones (total: 6)\tThese items may be found by defeating foes in Imlad Morgul instances. Different instances will yield different types of items.\n2\tReturn to Tordoron\tYou should deliver the items you collected to Tordoron in Echad Uial.\n",
[14285]="7005559C\n1\tCollect Morgul plaster (total: 6)\030Collect treated dowels (total: 6)\tThese items may be found by defeating foes in Imlad Morgul instances. Different instances will yield different types of items.\n2\tReturn to Tordoron\tYou should deliver the items you collected to Tordoron in Echad Uial.\n",
[14286]="7004A900\n1\tDefeat enemies in Lhingris (total: 20)\tMany kinds of insects and spiders can be found in Lhingris. You should defeat spiders and insects.\n",
[14287]="700272BB\n1\tScout Ak-ghru\tThe clear-cut forest can be found at Ak-ghru. Elfrith asked you to investigate the clear-cut part of the forest to determine how much wood the Orcs have gathered.\n2\tTalk to Elfrith\tElfrith is hiding beyond the bounds of Ak-ghru. You should report to Elfrith that the Orcs have cut a large amount of wood, probably for use in building siege-engines.\n",
[14288]="7002F005\n1\tHelp Thane Utred make his decision\tThane Utred must decide whether to defend or evacuate Langhold.\n2\tSpeak with Dala\tDala stands at Tunbert's farm near Langhold. You should speak with Dala.\n",
[14289]="700173C7\n1\tDefeat Gazathrug Enforcers (total: 6)\030Defeat Gazathrug Lurkers (total: 3)\tThe Orcs can be found at the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch. Avar has tasked you with defeating the Orcs who guard the throne of Igash.\n2\tTalk to Avar at the Orc-watch\tAvar is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair. You should return to Avar with news of your success.\n",
[14290]="70001742\n1\tDestroy Hillman weapons rack (total: 4)\030Destroy Hillman shield rack (total: 4)\030Destroy Hillman food crates (total: 6)\tThe food stores, weapons, and shields can be found in the northern part of the Hillmen's camp, north-east of Esteldín. You should destroy the food stores, weapons, and shields of the Hillmen, affecting their ability to effectively wage war.\n2\tCompleted\tYou found and destroyed the weapons, armour, and food stores of the Hillmen in an effort to slow their progress and ability to field a true army. You have done the Rangers of Esteldín a great service.\n",
[14291]="700372D8\n1\tTalk to Baldmund\030Talk to Grimmar\030Talk to Ordlac\030Talk to Dudsig\tGrimmar and Ordlac are in the Mead Hall of Stoke. Baldmund is at the inn in the north-eastern part of Stoke. Dudsig is at the Oserley encampment outside the north-east gate of Stoke. Reeve Fríthild has asked you to speak with the leaders of the forces at Stoke and learn what their advice for her would be.\n2\tBaldmund, Grimmar, Ordlac, and Dudsig have need of your services. You should give them your aid.\t\n3\tComplete Ordlac's Advice\tOrdlac is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. You should wait for Ordlac's advice to be heard.\n4\tTalk to Fríthild\tFríthild is in the Mead Hall of Stoke. You should return to Fríthild with the town leaders' advice.\n",
[14292]="7006EEDB\n1\tSpeak with the messenger from Khûd Zagin near the back gate\tSpeak with the messenger from Khûd Zagin near the back gate.\n2\tDeliver Amalíbi's message to Mizâdi\tDeliver Amalíbi's message to Mizâdi.\n3\tSpeak with Usanâb from Khûd Zagin\tSpeak with Usanâb from Khûd Zagin.\n4\tDeliver Usanâb's final message to Mizâdi in Kûr Anzar\tDeliver Usanâb's final message to Mizâdi in Kûr Anzar.\n5\tGather fallen weapons for the Subuzûri in Kûr Anzar (total: 8)\030Gather provisions for the waggons going south in Kûr Anzar (total: 10)\tGather fallen weapons for the Subuzûri and provisions for the waggons going south from around Kûr Anzar.\n6\tDeposit supplies in the waggon outside the back gate\tDeposit supplies in the waggon outside the back gate.\n7\tSpeak with Mizâdi in Kûr Anzar\tSpeak with Mizâdi in Kûr Anzar.\n",
[14293]="7001D0CC\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Gathbúrz (total: 15)\tOrcs can be found throughout Gathbúrz. Rodelleth has bidden you lay waste to the Orc-soldiers garrisoning Gathbúrz, to hinder their own imminent assault upon Lothlórien.\n2\tTalk to Rodelleth in Thangúlhad\tRodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz. You should return to Rodelleth with news of your success.\n",
[14294]="70040D16\n1\tDefeat corsair hound-masters and war-hounds\tWar-hounds and their Corsair handlers can be found at Abedec's Watch in southern Belfalas. You should battle the war-hounds and the Corsairs who act as their brutal masters.\n2\tDefeat corsair hound-masters (total: 5)\030Defeat evil war-hounds (total: 10)\tWar-hounds and their Corsair handlers can be found at Abedec's Watch in southern Belfalas. You should battle the war-hounds and the Corsairs who act as their brutal masters.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the evil war-hounds prowling with their masters in Abedec's Watch.\n",
[14295]="70037BE8\n1\tDestroy siege machines (total: 3)\tThere are ballistae shooting at the towers and Brockbridge defenders. They must be destroyed.\n2\tComplete\tYour actions gave the defenders a brief rest from the threat of the siege machines.\n",
[14296]="70030870\n1\tDefeat Mordor Orc-workers (total: 8)\tNîn-stazg is south-east of Floodwend, just out of sight of the town's walls. You should defeat Orcs at Nîn-stazg to thin their ranks.\n2\tCompleted\tThe forces of Mordor will employ their Orc-slaves for any task, be it soldiers in war or mindless workers to chop wood and assemble weapons. As long as the Orcs endure, the Enemy will never cease to have power.\n",
[14297]="70035A75\n1\tDefeat Arataus\tArataus and his band of riders roam the plains on the eastern side of The Fallows.\n2\tCompleted\tArataus and his band of riders roam the plains on the eastern side of The Fallows.\n",
[14298]="70035A80\n1\tDefeat Balcharan\tBalcharan and his minions have been terrorizing the people of Writhendowns and must be dealt with.\n2\tCompleted\tBalcharan and his minions have been terrorizing the people of Writhendowns and must be dealt with.\n",
[14299]="70035A7C\n1\tDefeat Conog\tConog can be found patrolling the southern Whitshaws with a horde of White Hand minions.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Conog, earning the gratitude of the people of Wildermore.\n",
[14300]="70035A7E\n1\tDefeat Foulwing\tFoulwing and his minions have been terrorizing the people of Writhendowns and must be dealt with.\n2\tCompleted\tFoulwing and his minions have been terrorizing the people of Writhendowns and must be dealt with.\n",
[14301]="70035A7D\n1\tDefeat Gîmtog\tGîmtog can be found patrolling the eastern edge of the Whitshaws with a pack of vicious wolves.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Gîmtog, earning the gratitude of the people of Wildermore.\n",
[14302]="70035A7B\n1\tDefeat Karkas\tKarkas can be found stomping throughout the hills of the High Knolls.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Karkas, earning the trust of the people of Wildermore.\n",
[14303]="70035A78\n1\tDefeat Rottenheart\tRottenheart can be found in south-western Balewood atop a snowy hill. The Huorn, Rottenheart, is an uncontrollable force of nature, and a danger to all that dwell within Balewood.\n2\tCompleted\tThe Huorn, Rottenheart, is an uncontrollable force of nature, and a danger to all that dwell within Balewood.\n",
[14304]="70035A77\n1\tDefeat Shaguk\tShaguk and his band of riders roam the plains on the eastern side of The Fallows.\n2\tCompleted\tShaguk and his band of riders roam the plains on the eastern side of The Fallows.\n",
